  "literature_notes": "All five ledger lines (L1\u2013L5) describe N-terminal tags (GFP, His-eGFP, FLAG) on full-length OTOP3 or its close Xenopus ortholog XtOTOP3. The topology landmarks place the N-terminus (residues 1\u201388) entirely on the intracellular face, with TM1 beginning at residue 89. L3 provides direct experimental confirmation: the N-terminal GFP is resistant to extracellular protease before permeabilization and is only cleaved after digitonin treatment, establishing 'N-terminus inside orientation'. Because every ledger-supported insertion is intracellular, zero extracellular surface tag sites qualify. The six extracellular loops (112\u2013120, 183\u2013193, 249\u2013289, 359\u2013372, 437\u2013448, 550\u2013563) have no ledger support for any insertion whatsoever and cannot be proposed.",
